From 3407af72d887e315f883c7b2abc877895036071f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:02:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] icm45686-spi and i2spi-chain: SlimeVR's IMUs on I2SPI chains

icm45686-spi is 0024's ICM-45686 on SPI: the chip (registers, FIFO,
motion, attitude) moves into a core both types share, and the SPI side
adds framing (register byte, bit 7 to read; bursts as on I2C) and
"fights": bytes moved while another icm45686-spi was selected too. Both
types gain "frames-read", the FIFO frames a host has read.

i2spi-chain is an I2SPI chain (SPI data, I2C selection; docs/I2SPI.md in
HelaFaye/SlimeVR-Tracker-ESP): protocol v3 nodes behind one I2C address,
each channel gating an SPI part's chip select with the shared strobe, or
by SET_CS in software mode; identity reads; sensor power that starts off
and resets its parts when it comes on. "nodes", "links", "version" and
"misflash" set up a chain and its faults; "fights", "armed", "frames",
"arms" and "powered" read it back.

The qtest covers identity, power gating, one-hot arming, the strobe and
software chip selects, malformed frames, an empty cable, a mis-flashed
node, a deliberate two-select fight, and the FIFO over SPI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sb26stwPJiCMHhrBWZ2D9q
